From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:27:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: advertise scanout only for the formats a display
 presents

A build without GBM allocation has no allocator to ask whether a format
can be scanned out, and vrend_format_can_scanout() answered true for
every format. The capset's scanout mask then named all of them, NV12
and P010 among them, although the embedder's display presents only the
8-bit RGB layouts.

The guest believes the mask. minigbm keeps SCANOUT on a buffer
combination the mask names and strips it from the others. Its NV12
emulation over R8 buffers refuses a combination that has both emulation
and scanout, so the NV12 entry that kept SCANOUT was skipped ("Skipping
unsupported combination format:842094158"), as P010 was, and with it
went the video encoder, video decoder and camera uses that entry carried.

Without GBM allocation a format can now be scanned out only when it is
one of the eight B8G8R8A8, B8G8R8X8, A8R8G8B8, X8R8G8B8, R8G8B8A8,
X8B8G8R8, A8B8G8R8 and R8G8B8X8 layouts. A build with GBM allocation
still asks the allocator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 3e2d06cd1bc78eae59de5fddb26afba880d79e07..b929846e131e97b7136c584d8113509c8ac494c4 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -971,6 +971,27 @@ static inline bool vrend_format_is_ds(enum virgl_formats format)
    return tex_conv_table[format].bindings & VIRGL_BIND_DEPTH_STENCIL;
 }
 
+/* The 8-bit RGB layouts the embedder's display presents. A build without GBM
+ * allocation has no allocator to ask, so this is the whole set a scanout can
+ * be, and everything else, YUV above all, is not.
+ */
+static inline bool vrend_format_is_presented_rgb(enum virgl_formats format)
+{
+   switch (format) {
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM:
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_B8G8R8X8_UNORM:
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_A8R8G8B8_UNORM:
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_X8R8G8B8_UNORM:
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM:
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_X8B8G8R8_UNORM:
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_A8B8G8R8_UNORM:
+   case VIRGL_FORMAT_R8G8B8X8_UNORM:
+      return true;
+   default:
+      return false;
+   }
+}
+
 static inline bool vrend_format_can_scanout(enum virgl_formats format)
 {
 #if defined(HAVE_EPOXY_EGL_H) && defined(ENABLE_GBM_ALLOCATION)
@@ -983,8 +1004,7 @@ static inline bool vrend_format_can_scanout(enum virgl_formats format)
 
    return gbm_device_is_format_supported(gbm->device, gbm_format, GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT);
 #else
-   (void)format;
-   return true;
+   return vrend_format_is_presented_rgb(format);
 #endif
 }
 
